  "explanation": "First find $g(4) = \\frac{4+3}{4-2} = \\frac{7}{2}$ and $g(1) = \\frac{1+3}{1-2} = \\frac{4}{-1} = -4$. Then $g(4) - g(1) = \\frac{7}{2} - (-4) = \\frac{7}{2} + 4 = \\frac{7}{2} + \\frac{8}{2} = \\frac{15}{2}$.\n\nWhy A is incorrect:\n\nResults from a sign error, computing $g(4) - g(1)$ as $\\frac{7}{2} - 4$ instead of $\\frac{7}{2} - (-4)$, giving $\\frac{7}{2} - \\frac{8}{2} = -\\frac{1}{2}$.",
